    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "When working with html tags, by context I mean attributes\r\n```html\r\n<div class=\"cool\" id=\"stuff\">\r\n...\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo in https://github.com/tpope/vim-surround for example I have two options to replace the div tag which is to replace it entirely with `cst<` then the tag name and closing bracket (example `span>` which produces this result\r\n```\r\n<span>\r\n...\r\n</span>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe second option is keeping the class and id attributes which can be done with `cst<` as well but then when you do only the tag name `span` it will keep the attributes so produces the following result\r\n```\r\n<span class=\"cool\" id=\"stuff\">\r\n...\r\n</span>\r\n```",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">When working with html tags, by context I mean attributes</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"&lt;div class=&quot;cool&quot; id=&quot;stuff&quot;&gt;\n...\n&lt;/div&gt;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">class</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">cool</span>\" <span class=\"pl-c1\">id</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">stuff</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n...\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">div</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So in <a href=\"https://github.com/tpope/vim-surround\">https://github.com/tpope/vim-surround</a> for example I have two options to replace the div tag which is to replace it entirely with <code class=\"notranslate\">cst&lt;</code> then the tag name and closing bracket (example <code class=\"notranslate\">span&gt;</code> which produces this result</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"&lt;span&gt;\n...\n&lt;/span&gt;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;span&gt;\n...\n&lt;/span&gt;\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The second option is keeping the class and id attributes which can be done with <code class=\"notranslate\">cst&lt;</code> as well but then when you do only the tag name <code class=\"notranslate\">span</code> it will keep the attributes so produces the following result</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"&lt;span class=&quot;cool&quot; id=&quot;stuff&quot;&gt;\n...\n&lt;/span&gt;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;span class=\"cool\" id=\"stuff\"&gt;\n...\n&lt;/span&gt;\n</code></pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "When working with html tags, by context I mean attributes\n<div class=\"cool\" id=\"stuff\">\n...\n</div>\nSo in https://github.com/tpope/vim-surround for example I have two options to replace the div tag which is to replace it entirely with cst< then the tag name and closing bracket (example span> which produces this result\n<span>\n...\n</span>\n\nThe second option is keeping the class and id attributes which can be done with cst< as well but then when you do only the tag name span it will keep the attributes so produces the following result\n<span class=\"cool\" id=\"stuff\">\n...\n</span>",
