            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The `t` (tag) surrounding will always delete/replace the whole tag with all attributes inside. The approach here for adjusting only tag name is to create a separate surrounding specifically for this. For example, under `T` surrounding as [described here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1293#issuecomment-2423827325). With this, you can `srTT` to replace tag name with another tag name.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">t</code> (tag) surrounding will always delete/replace the whole tag with all attributes inside. The approach here for adjusting only tag name is to create a separate surrounding specifically for this. For example, under <code class=\"notranslate\">T</code> surrounding as <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1293#issuecomment-2423827325\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1293/hovercard\">described here</a>. With this, you can <code class=\"notranslate\">srTT</code> to replace tag name with another tag name.</p>",
            "bodyText": "The t (tag) surrounding will always delete/replace the whole tag with all attributes inside. The approach here for adjusting only tag name is to create a separate surrounding specifically for this. For example, under T surrounding as described here. With this, you can srTT to replace tag name with another tag name.",
